# CSS (recap-engine)

Global BEM with a `recap-` namespace (not CSS Modules). Isolates styles inside host apps.

## Naming

```css
.recap-{block} { }
.recap-{block}__{element} { }
.recap-{block}--{modifier} { }
```

- Default block = kebab-case component name: `Stat` → `recap-stat`
- Shared affordances may shorten (`recap-btn`) — document why and reuse from multiple components
- Motion: `recap-motion--{preset}`; block effects: `recap-{block}--{effect}`
- Never ship unprefixed classes from the library

```css
/* ❌ BAD */
.stat-value { color: #fff; }

/* ✅ GOOD */
.recap-stat__value { color: var(--recap-fg); }
```

## Tokens

- Theme via `--recap-*` on `.recap-root` (`styles/root.css`)
- Primitives use tokens, not hardcoded brand colors (fallbacks only in `root.css`)
- Duration / easing from `--recap-motion-*` when shared

## Colocation

- Component-owned rules → `ComponentName/styles.css`
- Shared scene / motion / tokens → `src/styles/`
- New stylesheet → add `@import` in `src/styles.css`
- No empty CSS files; wrappers that reuse `recap-btn` do not add their own sheet

## Consumers

Document: `import '@recap-engine/react/styles.css'`
